# No `index.ts` / `index.tsx` for component folders

**Never** create `index.ts` or `index.tsx` (or `index.js` / `index.jsx`) as a barrel or re-export entry for a React component folder.

## Required pattern

- Name the main component file after the feature, e.g. `recipe-header/recipe-header.tsx` exporting `RecipeHeader`.
- Import with the **full path** to that file:

```ts
import { RecipeHeader } from '@/app/.../recipe-header/recipe-header';
```

## Folder layout

```text
_components/
  recipe-header/
    recipe-header.tsx          ← entry; exports RecipeHeader
    recipe-header-actions.tsx
    recipe-header-badges.tsx
    use-recipe-header-display.ts
```

## Do not

```text
❌ recipe-header/index.tsx      ← re-exports RecipeHeader
❌ import { RecipeHeader } from '.../recipe-header'   ← relies on index resolution
```

Split files (`recipe-header-meta.tsx`, hooks, helpers) stay as separate named modules. Only the **primary** component file acts as the public entry — not an index barrel.

Works with [`modular-components.mdc`](modular-components.mdc) and [`nextjs-app-file-organization.mdc`](nextjs-app-file-organization.mdc).
